{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqg67dvm816","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"VERIFIED LIVE: background-worker write-gate fixed daemon-side; subagent dispatch works without orch-off","summary":"Update to note-mqg3f5bdzua. The background-worker write-gate denial is FIXED and verified live as of 2026-06-16 (main HEAD 77488f2), with NO Claude Desktop / MCP-server restart required.\n\nFIX: routes/overlay.js in_progress claim handler now falls back to the daemon's own process.env.CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID when no session resolves from b.session_id / agent registry. The daemon inherits CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID via daemonEnv (={...MCP-server env}); under claude-desktop it equals the worker's harness .session_id that the PreToolUse gate queries /active-claim with, so a hookless background-worker claim becomes gate-visible. Activates on a DAEMON restart (which a kill→ensureDaemon-respawn does), unlike the equivalent mcp-graph SESSION fix which needs an MCP-server reload.\n\nVERIFICATION (end-to-end, real background subagent): branch_task(\"7\") → start_task(\"7\", agent_id, NO session_id) → {ok} → Write inside the worktree SUCCEEDED (no orch-gate denial) → complete_task ok. This is the exact path that was denied for the CE-1 worker (note-mqftffo7f2b). Throwaway task #7 + worktree cleaned up after.\n\nIMPLICATION: the documented dispatch contract (branch_task → start_task → commit → complete_task) now works for run_in_background Agent-tool workers without passing session_id and without orch-off. The orch-off/inline workaround for orchestrator-source edits is no longer required. Note: relies on workers sharing the harness session id (probe-verified for this setup); a harness giving workers distinct sessions would need the worker to pass its own session_id explicitly. The mcp-graph.js SESSION fallback (also merged) is the conceptual home and kicks in too once the app restarts.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T04:57:11.938Z","vec":[-0.12159837037324905,